  {
   "at": [
    "apps",
    "workspace"
   ],
   "name": "text",
   "id": "workspace-text",
   "value": "a workspace: text kept in the graph, at /apps/workspace/text.\n\ncmd-s saves it. Open any node in an editor from the graph browser (alt-g, then enter),\nor from a shell: edit /programs/status.\n"
  },
  {
   "at": [
    "home"
   ],
   "name": "Welcome",
   "id": "home-welcome",
   "value": "Welcome to your computer.\n\nThis is your home, /home. What you keep here stays on this\nmachine's card, and goes wherever you share it.\n\n  Notes      for writing things down; cmd-n makes a new note\n  Pictures   a few to start with: open one, then Set as Desktop\n  Trash      what you throw away waits here until you empty it\n\nDouble-click to open. The arrow at the top left goes up a\nfolder; the path at the bottom goes anywhere, as far as /, the\nwhole graph. Every folder here is a node, and so is every file:\na node can hold a value and other nodes at once.\n\nConnect... mounts a node someone shared with you: paste the id\ntheir share printed, give it a name, and it shows up here, live.\n\nHave a lovely day.\n"
  },
  {
   "at": [
    "home"
   ],
   "name": "Notes",
   "id": "home-notes",
   "value": null
  },
  {
   "at": [
    "home",
    "Notes"
   ],
   "name": "Things to try",
   "id": "home-notes-try",
   "value": "Things to try\n\n- write a note and save it with cmd-s\n- make a folder for a project\n- set the gingham as your desktop\n- open / and wander about: everything on this machine is a node\n"
  },
